WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
Given the astounding success&nbsp;
of The Last of Us, hopefully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.800
this gives studios a much better outlook&nbsp;
on wanting to do high-quality video game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.360
adaptations. And ones that are actually&nbsp;
faithful to the source material. That’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.080
the major distinction because there’s been&nbsp;
a lot so far that don’t follow the source&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.700
material at all *cough* Halo *cough* and The&nbsp;
Last of Us is proof that there is a ton of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:25.860
unmined potential within the video game sphere&nbsp;
because we are basically just getting started.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:30.900
For the first game on this list, since The Last of&nbsp;
Us has had groundbreaking success, it only makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:36.540
sense to adapt God of War. Initially, upon writing&nbsp;
this I didn’t even know that Amazon acquired the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:41.640
rights to do an adaptation of God of War back&nbsp;
in December 2022. There haven’t really been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:45.660
any updates about it, so I’ll still go into&nbsp;
why this could make such a great adaptation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:51.300
even though it’s announced. Now this would be a&nbsp;
very challenging game to adapt given how huge the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:56.280
scale of it is. Along with the budget probably&nbsp;
needing to be massive. Out of all the studios&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.840
to acquire it though, Amazon would most likely&nbsp;
be willing to write a blank check for the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:05.820
given that The Rings of Power costed over&nbsp;
a billion dollars. However, if they didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:11.100
want to casually drop another billion dollars,&nbsp;
you could start the show at God of War 2018.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.360
The budget will still need to be pretty large,&nbsp;
but at least the story will be more manageable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:21.420
to tell at a slightly smaller scale in comparison&nbsp;
to the first three games. Given that at its core,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:26.520
it’s primarily a father and son adventure. So&nbsp;
that's a pretty easy story to tackle for a show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:32.580
format. Kratos and Atreus are complex characters&nbsp;
and their rich dynamic will anchor down the story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:38.100
Kratos learns to become a better father and opens&nbsp;
up to his son, while Atreus learns to become more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:42.600
mature and to be more like a warrior. There’s a&nbsp;
strong progression for both of these characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:48.060
so every dialogue scene they have together should&nbsp;
be very engaging. That’s one thing that most video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:53.160
game adaptations require. If it doesn’t have a&nbsp;
strong base story with great characters, then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:58.020
it would be really hard to translate it over to&nbsp;
shows and movies. Like the biggest example of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:03.480
is Doom. There really isn’t much of a story or&nbsp;
characters in Doom, and is predominantly carried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:09.240
by its gameplay. It does have some cool background&nbsp;
lore, but you also need a great plot. For shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:14.460
and movies, you can’t just have non-stop action&nbsp;
with barely any dialogue. Because if you do that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:18.480
you won’t be able to form an attachment to&nbsp;
the characters and the audience will slowly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.340
stop caring about the narrative. A good story&nbsp;
makes you care about the action and without one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:27.960
you won’t be invested or have any stakes in&nbsp;
the action. So on the other side of this coin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:33.360
you have God of War. Two loveable characters&nbsp;
who go on a fun journey across the realms. Any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:37.620
action along the way is investing because you&nbsp;
like the characters and you want to see them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:42.000
achieve their goal. I just wanted to quickly go&nbsp;
over that, because I won’t be including games&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.740
that are solely based on good gameplay. Going&nbsp;
into how much meat God of War has to offer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:52.260
you can easily do a whole season per game. At&nbsp;
least pertaining to the last two God of Wars. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:55.980
think there’s enough there and even though there&nbsp;
are some repetitive sections within those games,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:01.140
you can cut them out and tighten up the pace for&nbsp;
the narrative. I also think that choosing God of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:05.940
War 2018 as a starting point will make Kratos&nbsp;
an even more intriguing character given how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:11.160
mysterious his past is. Because throughout the&nbsp;
game the writers allude to what happened in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:15.900
past. So if anything, skipping the first three&nbsp;
games won’t hinder the overall story because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:20.760
God of War 2018 essentially hits the restart&nbsp;
button. You can start it at the very beginning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:25.740
and go into the tragedy of Kratos’ origin, but&nbsp;
you’ll have to make some heavy changes to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:30.120
story because I’d assume viewers won’t want to&nbsp;
watch Kratos go to the underworld three separate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:34.740
times. Out of all of the adaptations I’ll be&nbsp;
going into, this is at the top of my list.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:40.380
Another dream come true would be a proper&nbsp;
adaptation of Halo. Since the Paramount + show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:45.540
doesn’t exist to me. Now this is much harder&nbsp;
material to adapt in comparison to other games&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:50.340
given that Master Chief is kind of just a&nbsp;
vessel for the player. He has extremely light&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:55.620
characterization and only Halo 4 really makes&nbsp;
an effort to humanize him. So telling his story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.620 --> 00:04:00.420
if anything kind of feels like a trap. You’d&nbsp;
either have to make major changes to the source&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:05.160
material to make Master Chief more of a character&nbsp;
similar to the Paramount Plus show so that you can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:10.260
sympathize and relate to him. But also not like&nbsp;
the show where they make him overly emotional,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:15.720
he barely has his helmet on, and they even give&nbsp;
him nude scenes. Or if you don’t make any changes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:21.120
to Master Chief, you have a main protagonist that&nbsp;
barely talks. I keep seeing people say that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.380
would love a show with this faithfulness to&nbsp;
Chief, but again, without a proper character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:29.940
to be attached to who barely speaks or emotes,&nbsp;
then the story will have a hard time operating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:35.100
Games can get away with this because it’s more&nbsp;
objective based and you become the character. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:40.200
shows and movies, we witness the story without&nbsp;
having any input. Since Master Chief would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.640
very difficult to adapt without ruining him,&nbsp;
I would recommend adapting a story within the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:49.620
Halo universe that doesn’t involve Chief, or at&nbsp;
least doesn’t make him the main character. That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:54.000
may be a controversial opinion, but that also&nbsp;
seems to be the most realistic and easiest of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.380
the options. There’s also a lot of material to&nbsp;
choose from that doesn’t even include Master&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:03.960
Chief, but I’ll only look at the existing games.&nbsp;
Currently the most adaptable and that also happens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:09.840
to be one of the best stories is Halo: Reach.&nbsp;
This is an outstanding setting and witnessing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:15.360
a society collapse from an alien invasion is&nbsp;
awesome. Halo: Reach also has a good roster of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:20.400
characters. Now they aren’t as rich as the main&nbsp;
characters in The Last of Us and God of War, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:25.200
it wouldn’t betray the source material to expand&nbsp;
upon these characters. They’re all pretty distinct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:29.040
and varied, so you’ll be able to make for some&nbsp;
good pairings throughout the miniseries. Which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:34.080
is what I think Halo: Reach will fit the best as.&nbsp;
Each mission would lend pretty well to a separate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:37.800
episode given that they are consistently&nbsp;
changing settings. And in each episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:42.840
they can spend time developing a certain character&nbsp;
within the squad with the main character. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:47.520
for the main character, he doesn’t have much of a&nbsp;
personality and is even more of a vessel for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:52.560
player than Master Chief, so you’ll have to change&nbsp;
him and make him an actual character. You can lean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:57.240
into how he’s pitched as in the game in which&nbsp;
he’s a lone wolf with a mysterious past. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:02.040
could naturally offer as a point of conflict&nbsp;
between the main character and the team, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:07.140
through the story he learns the value of teamwork&nbsp;
and is reinvigorated by the camaraderie of his new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:12.180
family. Thus changing him into a character with&nbsp;
more heart and someone with warmth. At first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:16.620
he could be doubtful about the effectiveness of&nbsp;
his team and attempts to get things done on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:21.060
own in a selfish manner and is more closed&nbsp;
off. Then through the course of the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:26.400
all these negative aspects are peeled away through&nbsp;
different selfless and kind acts made by his team.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:31.620
I think this could offer a solid character arc&nbsp;
for Noble Six and can easily add a deeper layer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:35.760
to him. That and you don’t have to make him the&nbsp;
main character since he’ll inherently be a bit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:39.420
unlikable towards the beginning. If you went with&nbsp;
this pitch. So instead, you could mostly focus on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:43.680
the squad as a whole, while slowly pivoting&nbsp;
towards Noble Six as being the main point of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:48.540
view who is slowly winning the hearts of the&nbsp;
audience. The overall story arc for Halo Reach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:52.920
is pretty great and I would go into more depth&nbsp;
about it, but that would be going into spoilers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:56.400
and I kind of want to stay away from them&nbsp;
in this video since I’ll be touching on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:02.040
a wide array of games. But the story acts as&nbsp;
a mad dash to save humanity and the squad we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:07.620
follow are integral in that goal and the actions&nbsp;
they make carry a massive amount of weight. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:12.900
can easily be a very epic, fun, and emotional&nbsp;
journey carried out by this lovable squad of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:17.940
spartans. It’s just really depressing that this&nbsp;
probably won’t come to fruition for a while given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:22.560
that Paramount + is doing their own show and&nbsp;
that doesn’t even follow the source material.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:31.680
Dead Space. This is a game that I’m genuinely&nbsp;
surprised hasn’t been adapted into a horror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:37.020
movie yet, or even hearing any development around&nbsp;
a possible movie. Because between everything on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:41.940
this list, this is probably the easiest material&nbsp;
to adapt because of the simple premise of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:47.220
game. This crew responds to a distress signal&nbsp;
in space and they are met with nightmarish and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:52.200
eldritch horrors and the crew then has to&nbsp;
escape. The premise in of itself is perfect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:58.080
for a movie and the atmosphere in the game is&nbsp;
extremely immersive. The dilapidating interiors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:03.600
blood-soaked and terrifying displays of gore and&nbsp;
body horror strewn throughout the environment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:07.800
creepy lighting and atmosphere that&nbsp;
always hammers home a feeling of dread,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:13.260
this is literally a perfect horror environment.&nbsp;
In the hands of a competent horror director, this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:18.960
should be a surefire hit. Even though the premise&nbsp;
itself isn’t entirely original, the designs of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:24.060
the monsters and how everything operates is very&nbsp;
intriguing. Like the mystery behind the Marker and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:28.680
how it affects people would constantly keep a hook&nbsp;
in the audience. Along with it potentially being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:34.080
cool visually how the filmmakers would portray&nbsp;
the hysteria induced by the Marker. As for how the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:38.760
story of the game translates to a movie, it should&nbsp;
definitely be cut down because the game is mostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:44.040
a string of objectives of repairing the Ishimura.&nbsp;
Having to repair basically the entire ship was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:49.500
mostly a story mechanic to artificially elongate&nbsp;
the game. This is fine for the game because they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:54.420
keep introducing new gameplay elements to keep&nbsp;
things fresh and interesting. But for a movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:58.920
you need to keep the narrative moving at&nbsp;
a satisfying pace. So any filmmaker would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:03.600
definitely need to cut it down and from there, you&nbsp;
could cherry-pick the many horror set pieces from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:08.340
the game. That and the climax is pretty insane&nbsp;
so the ending should definitely still be great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:13.200
for the movie. In terms of budget, it should&nbsp;
definitely be pretty manageable because most of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:18.180
the game takes place in closed interiors. Meaning&nbsp;
that you could shoot all of this on enclosed sets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:23.220
on a soundstage. The amount of VFX shouldn’t&nbsp;
be too crazy and I’d much prefer to see some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:28.500
practical necromorphs. If any filmmaker were to&nbsp;
go with solely VFX necromorphs then that would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:33.480
be extremely saddening. But overall, I’d assume&nbsp;
this will probably be adapted soon especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:38.280
since the popularity around the game has surged&nbsp;
from the outstanding reception of the remake.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:44.340
Bioshock. Now this game has been blueballing&nbsp;
gamers because there has been news about a movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:49.860
for this game ranging back to pre-2010. Studios&nbsp;
were scared to make the movie because making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:55.920
a very high-budget R-rated movie seemed like a&nbsp;
guaranteed flop. However, a year and a half ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:00.060
it was announced that this game is actually&nbsp;
being developed by Netflix in a partnership&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:05.580
with 2k games. It’s being directed by Francis&nbsp;
Lawrence who directed the last 3 Hunger Games and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:10.680
I am Legend. So it’s in the hands of a competent&nbsp;
director and the studio that developed the game is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:15.180
involved. The only thing about this adaptation&nbsp;
though and why I’m including this is that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:19.560
haven’t received much updates about this project&nbsp;
and that makes me worried given what happened in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:24.780
the past. But going into why Bioshock would make&nbsp;
a magnificent adaptation is because it checks off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:31.140
a lot boxes. The world of Rapture is incredibly&nbsp;
immersive and is a constant visual feast. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:35.820
underwater city lends itself to so many unique and&nbsp;
cool setpieces of withering structures that have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:40.860
so much environmental storytelling. The entire&nbsp;
background behind the architecture is just so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:45.660
intriguing and so is all of the story surrounding&nbsp;
it. This could lead to such a thought-provoking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:50.160
script because the world is constantly oozing&nbsp;
with so much subtext about what happened to this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:56.400
dystopian society. It has engaging themes like&nbsp;
that of class, inequality, unchecked capitalism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:01.560
and abuse of power leading to the fall of this&nbsp;
city. There’s also a lot of vibrant and unhinged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:05.280
characters throughout this world and given&nbsp;
that there’s so much dialogue communicated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:10.020
over a radio, there should never be any down&nbsp;
moments within the script. Along with there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:14.460
being an outstanding twist towards the end of the&nbsp;
game that completely shatters your perception of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:19.020
the story. Then there’s also the brilliant&nbsp;
designs of the augmented humans like slicers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:24.540
and big daddys that would be so cool to see done&nbsp;
in live action. Really every aspect about the game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:29.760
carried over into a movie or mini-series setting&nbsp;
will be an instant classic. So hopefully Netflix&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:35.400
actually commits to making this project and gives&nbsp;
them a big enough budget. Because another thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:40.140
that makes me really excited about the Netflix&nbsp;
adaptation is that it’s being written by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:45.720
writer of Blade Runner 2049. That pace and overall&nbsp;
aesthetic from that movie would fit perfectly in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:51.240
Bioshock, and if they somehow got Roger Deakins&nbsp;
as the cinematographer then I’d probably pass out.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:57.180
Resident Evil 7. This would be a pretty simple&nbsp;
adaptation honestly and the main reason why I’m&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.180 --> 00:12:02.580
choosing the 7th entry is because A. It’s not an&nbsp;
overly complex story and is mainly about surviving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:07.740
this crazy family, and B. There’s been a lot of&nbsp;
failed adaptations for the first couple of games,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:12.480
so I’d like to see them try some different&nbsp;
games in the franchise. I admittedly haven’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:17.400
played Resident Evil 4 yet and really want to,&nbsp;
so I wouldn’t be surprised if that would also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:22.980
make for a great movie as well. But for Resident&nbsp;
Evil 7, making it a pure horror movie of Ethan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:27.360
slowly trying to overcome this psychotic&nbsp;
hillbilly family with powers would make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:33.060
for a riveting ride. It’s also extremely similar&nbsp;
to the original Texas Chainsaw Massacre so the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:37.920
story already should function within a movie or&nbsp;
mini-series format. If it were in a mini-series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:42.720
format, you can have each episode where Ethan&nbsp;
overcomes one of the members of the family and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:47.640
thus becomes more hardened as a character. Or&nbsp;
if it were a movie, you can condense down some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:52.860
of the setpieces a bit and make it a perfect 2&nbsp;
hours. Like ideally probably cut out the whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:58.500
boat sequence which felt weird and try to tackle&nbsp;
the same story revelation in a different manner. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:03.000
would go into that more, but I’m refraining from&nbsp;
going into spoilers. Talking about it vaguely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:07.020
though, the general background to this story&nbsp;
and how this family ended up the way they did,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:12.540
is really a tragedy and it uncovers a whole nother&nbsp;
layer to the story that gives it a lot of depth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:16.500
and doesn’t just make this family a&nbsp;
bunch of psychos. It makes them a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:20.880
more sympathetic and by the end of the game,&nbsp;
you kind of just feel bad for them. The main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:24.960
character would probably need a little bit more&nbsp;
characterization, but at the end of the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:29.340
it is really a story of survival and that&nbsp;
always is a great time for horror movies.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:35.460
Overwatch. I’m honestly really surprised that&nbsp;
I even have to include this game because you’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:40.620
assume that Blizzard would have made an animated&nbsp;
movie or series by this point. Like the game has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:46.080
been out for seven years. God damn, I feel&nbsp;
old now. However, as I was making this video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:50.760
Blizzard did release an animated miniseries&nbsp;
for Overwatch. Although it’s extremely short&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:54.960
in length, and for that runtime, it was&nbsp;
pretty good. So the question stands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.960 --> 00:14:00.600
why the hell isn’t Blizzard contracting studios&nbsp;
to make longer-form content? It’s definitely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:06.540
not a money issue since Blizzard as a company is&nbsp;
reeling in 1 to 2 Billion dollars of net income a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:12.480
year. So greenlighting an animated series or movie&nbsp;
shouldn’t be that big of a deal. And if anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:18.060
it would just make them more money. It’s maddening&nbsp;
because the possibilities are truly endless and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:22.980
you could go into so many outstanding directions&nbsp;
for an Overwatch series. You could go the Arcane&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:27.600
route and make a rich and grounded drama and go&nbsp;
into the complexities of the world and select&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:32.700
characters. You could go down a more anthology&nbsp;
route where each episode follows one or a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:37.440
heroes as they carry out their most important&nbsp;
missions. Or you could even make the show like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:41.820
that amazing and epic Clone Wars show back&nbsp;
in the day, where you have massive battles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:46.500
with a huge scale. Literally, the possibilities&nbsp;
are endless and I’d assume you’d love to watch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:51.240
any of the three pitches I mentioned. So the&nbsp;
fact that we really have none of that is truly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:55.920
heartbreaking from the untapped potential. There&nbsp;
are so many cool and interesting characters that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.920 --> 00:15:00.660
I would love to learn more about. The game only&nbsp;
scratches the surface for these characters in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:04.920
terms of development and it feels like fans have&nbsp;
been blueballed for so long in terms of getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:09.600
to know them more. For me personally, I only know&nbsp;
the surface level for each of the characters in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:14.400
Overwatch and I would love to get a deep dive and&nbsp;
learn much more about them. That and the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:20.520
of Overwatch is definitely intriguing enough to&nbsp;
carry a show. So when Cuphead of all IPs gets 3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:25.860
seasons before Blizzard does practically anything&nbsp;
with Overwatch is really depressing. I don’t know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:30.000
what the hell management is doing over there and&nbsp;
surely all the money they’re milking out of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:35.220
players with absurd shop prices and battle passes&nbsp;
can give them enough money for a proper show.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:41.580
Red Dead Redemption 2. Out of Rockstar’s&nbsp;
catalogue, this seems like the best pick. Which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:46.380
isn’t downplaying GTA5 which could also make for&nbsp;
an interesting mini-series, but I think the story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:51.960
for Red Dead Redemption 2 is a bit better. A group&nbsp;
of outlaws who are all colorful and sympathetic in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:56.760
their own way would make for a fun perspective&nbsp;
to follow for a big sprawling adventure. They’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.760 --> 00:16:01.980
all essentially antiheroes and morally complex&nbsp;
characters who aren’t just good or bad and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:06.900
makes riveting subjects in my opinion. Along with&nbsp;
the deep dynamics and synergies between all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:11.400
them. The main reason why I’m bringing up Red Dead&nbsp;
Redemption 2 besides the fact that it has a great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:16.500
story, is that Westerns in general have really&nbsp;
fallen off over the years. Which is kind of sad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:22.020
to be honest. They used to be so dominant back&nbsp;
in the day and there are only a small handful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:26.760
of good Westerns that have come out in the last&nbsp;
10 years. So it would be really exciting to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:31.680
a big return to this genre that would ideally&nbsp;
be followed by a big budget. Which this would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:37.200
also kind of be a first in that we don’t have that&nbsp;
many other high-budget western period shows. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:42.540
only two that come to mind is Deadwood and Hell on&nbsp;
Wheels, so there is basically no competition right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:47.340
now for this area and I would love the variety.&nbsp;
That and I think Red Dead Redemption 2 could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.340 --> 00:16:52.440
find a really good balance between story/character&nbsp;
development and action. Given that there are many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:58.080
action setpieces in the game that could easily be&nbsp;
cherry-picked. But yeah, RDR2 seems like a pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:02.460
easy layup to the point that I’m surprised&nbsp;
no studios have taken an interest in it yet.

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:08.460
Little Nightmares. Now this may be a surprise&nbsp;
to you that I’m including this game and some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:12.600
of you may not have heard of Little Nightmares.&nbsp;
It’s an indie horror game in which you have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:18.600
navigate a hostile, malformed, and dark world with&nbsp;
horrors awaiting around every corner. The monster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:23.760
designs in this game are really unsettling&nbsp;
and plays into the childlike perspective of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:28.800
exaggerated horrors. The world is extremely&nbsp;
harsh and foreboding for you as a player and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:34.080
there is so much detail within the world that&nbsp;
that is the main driver for storytelling. Every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:38.640
environment tells a deeply tragic and dark&nbsp;
story that as you progress through the game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:43.080
it’s like you are slowly piecing together a&nbsp;
jigsaw puzzle as to what happened here. There’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:48.120
also no dialogue within the game so it makes the&nbsp;
mystery of this world that much more alluring. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:53.100
right away I think this would make for a perfect&nbsp;
stop-motion horror adventure. The crazy thing is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:58.500
that this project was actually being developed&nbsp;
and it was oddly enough being spearheaded by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:03.600
Anthony and Joe Russo. I honestly just chanced&nbsp;
upon the project as I was looking through their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:09.060
IMDB page. But the Little Nightmares adaptation&nbsp;
was going to be directed by the legendary Henry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:14.100
Selick who directed both The Nightmare Before&nbsp;
Christmas and Coraline. So the potential behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:19.320
this project was huge and it’s really depressing&nbsp;
that the project ended up fizzling out. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:24.120
this world fits perfectly for that kind of dark&nbsp;
stop-motion aesthetic. Along with the story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:28.260
actually being pretty riveting. Especially&nbsp;
for the second game in which there are some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:33.000
pretty big and surprising twists. So yeah, I&nbsp;
just wanted to call out this game since the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:37.500
world is so immersive and would be a really fun&nbsp;
adventure if the right talent wanted to make it.

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:43.860
Gears of War. Similar to Bioshock, it feels like&nbsp;
Gears of War has been in a perpetual development&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:43.860 --> 00:18:49.380
hell for adaptations. And again like Bioshock,&nbsp;
it seems that Netflix is stepping in and making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:54.060
it a reality. The main reason why I’m including&nbsp;
this game is that I really love the premise of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:59.340
the game and it could make for a cool gritty,&nbsp;
sci-fy, war epic. These kind of genre blends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:04.740
are really rare and that is why I’m craving it so&nbsp;
much and so are you most likely. Just like Halo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:09.000
fighting a war against an alien-like threat&nbsp;
where we are actively learning about them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:13.500
as the story goes on, makes the threat much&nbsp;
more terryfing. Along with there being cool&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:17.640
reveals for different enemy types throughout&nbsp;
the story to keep things fresh and exciting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:22.020
There’s so many fun and cool setpieces through&nbsp;
the initial trilogy to the point that they can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:26.280
definitely do a movie for each game. Like&nbsp;
I would love to see the worm setpiece from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:30.420
the second game without going into spoilers.&nbsp;
Then from a story and character perspective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:35.100
you can definitely create a pretty solid pace&nbsp;
since every character is pretty varied and iconic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:39.720
I’d love some actual sit-down scenes with these&nbsp;
characters since we don’t really get that from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:43.800
the games. All the dialogue is done while they&nbsp;
are walking through the world when they aren’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:48.840
engaged in combat. But each of their backstories&nbsp;
are deep enough to be explored to a good extent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:53.520
Like the main character, Marcus has an heir&nbsp;
of mystery to him in the first game as to why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:58.260
he’s locked up and what he did. Along with his&nbsp;
world views fundamentally contrasting different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:03.720
characters. That and his strict and mean persona&nbsp;
has a fun dynamic with other characters who are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:08.220
more lighthearted and fun. So from a world,&nbsp;
story, character, and action perspective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:13.440
this should be easily accomplishable with a good&nbsp;
budget that I hope Netflix commits to and actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:18.780
provides. Dave Bautista is practically begging&nbsp;
to be in the movie so please make that a reality.

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:22.860
Wolfenstein. Now for my last pick, there’s&nbsp;
quite a few games that I would love to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:28.440
like an Outlast horror movie, someone trying to&nbsp;
tackle the rich world of Half-life, or even a fun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:33.480
blockbuster Call of Duty action movie, but for&nbsp;
the last game I’ll talk about is Wolfenstein.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:38.040
And the reason why I’m choosing this game is that&nbsp;
I think this could be a very fun and over-the-top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:44.280
action movie or show. Given that the games have so&nbsp;
many crazy enemies like oversized robotic panzer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:50.160
hounds. Or colossal mechs that the Nazis somehow&nbsp;
made. It’s just such a batshit ridiculous concept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:54.720
that you can’t help but love how creative and fun&nbsp;
it is. So the style of filmmaking that I would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:54.720 --> 00:21:00.180
absolutely love to see attached to the Wolfenstein&nbsp;
franchise is Bollywood filmmaking. This would make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:05.220
a perfect pairing because the overexaggerated&nbsp;
aspects of action in those movies that clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:10.500
don’t follow logic and are just there to emphasize&nbsp;
and elevate the action past reality, would mix&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:15.720
perfectly with the crazy world of Wolfenstein.&nbsp;
Like I don’t care make Blaskowicz a fucking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:21.840
godlike entity in the game who can dual-wield&nbsp;
massive machine guns and solo the entire Nazi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:26.700
army. If you purely go off the rails with the&nbsp;
action, then the fans would adore this project.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:31.920
Now this story concept has been done before, but I&nbsp;
would love to see it done in this Bollywood action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:36.600
style. I know I said in the beginning of the video&nbsp;
that gameplay-dominated games won’t make for great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:41.580
adaptations, but I think Wolfenstein still has&nbsp;
a solid story. It fits in really well into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:46.080
story dynamic of an underdog and would make the&nbsp;
conflict that Blaskowicz has to overcome pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:50.760
riveting. Along with their being some vibrant&nbsp;
and fun characters along the way. It’s not like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:54.960
the games don’t have any story, because there’s&nbsp;
actually quite a bit of cinematic storytelling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:59.760
within this series. This obviously wouldn’t rival&nbsp;
like The Last of Us for storytelling quality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:04.440
but the action is the true highlight here. Because&nbsp;
who wouldn’t love watching Nazis get obliterated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:09.840
in the most insane ways possible. That would be&nbsp;
my dream from an action standpoint for this IP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:13.620
and from there you could really do whatever&nbsp;
you want with the story and depart from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:13.620 --> 00:22:17.820
games for all I care. The main game does have&nbsp;
a pretty iconic villain besides just Hitler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:17.820 --> 00:22:23.040
but you can really make any villain within that&nbsp;
world iconic with creative and out-there designs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:23.040 --> 00:22:28.260
So would anyone actually make this and would&nbsp;
this be a realistic dream? Probably not. I doubt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:28.260 --> 00:22:32.940
studios would actually have the balls to make&nbsp;
this, however, given that Twisted Metal didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:32.940 --> 00:22:37.980
really take itself seriously and was a fun joyride&nbsp;
then this type of adaptation could be possible.

